  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "On the latest update on 3/26/25 this was stated:\" If they are disabled while content is in the world, that content will be removed.\n\nEx: If there are Prints or Stickers in the world and you disable them, they will all be removed from the world.\"\n\nISSUE: \n\nHowever, if you are the Instance Master and try to remove the prints it will lag and then not remove the prints (we determined the lag might be from over 20+ people in the world). Sometimes it will remove the prints and other times it will not do it at all (20+ people?) .   We're not sure if it's because of too many people or too many prints.\n\nTRY IT OUT: \n\nCreate a world instance have 20+ people arrive and have some people print prints (lol).  Now, go into the option to turn the prints OFF and you'll get the \"Prints are now disabled\" message (sometimes delayed). You'll now see none of the prints disappear in a blue partical cloud.   \n\nAGAIN: \n\nDo the same as above but with LESS than 20 people and everything will work as stated on the release notes.",
